Psalm 4, Principle 1 ("Do not repay evil with evil") and Principle 2 ("Refrain from deceitful speech") find clear ethical equivalents in all seven other religions examined. The principle is expressed through different cultural lenses: as the command not to sin when disturbed (Psalm), as the virtue of those who are insulted and remain silent (Judaism), as the appeasement of hatred (Buddhism), as forgiveness sustaining the universe (Hinduism), as the reward of reconciliation (Islam), as conquering the inner enemy (Sikhism), as the mark of true humanity (Confucianism), and as the restoration of community harmony (African Traditional).

