| ****Principle 2: Evil Will Not Ultimately Prevail****                               | Those who act unjustly may prosper temporarily, but the moral order will not allow injustice to have the final word. Evil is self-defeating; the wicked are snared in the work of their own hands.     |
| ****Principle 3: Gratitude and Celebration Are Appropriate Responses to Justice**** | When justice is served, it is morally proper to give thanks, celebrate, and proclaim the goodness of the moral order.                                                                                  |

For our comparative purposes, ****Principle 1**** and ****Principle 2**** represent the most universally actionable ethical heuristics.

