| ****Principle 2: Moral Blindness Is a Form of Folly****                     | To deny the reality of the moral order is not wisdom but folly. It leads to self-destruction. The wise person acknowledges the moral order and seeks to live in accordance with it.                      |
| ****Principle 3: The Moral Order Will Vindicate the Righteous****           | Despite the apparent prosperity of the corrupt, the moral order will ultimately bring deliverance to the just. The righteous will rejoice.                                                               |

