Psalm 38, Principle 1 ("Acknowledgment of sin and guilt") and Principle 3 ("The silence of the suffering") find clear ethical equivalents in all seven other religions examined. The principles are expressed through different cultural lenses: as the psalmist's confession and silence (Psalm), as the Proverb's teaching on confession and mercy (Judaism), as the Buddhist teaching on self-examination and letting go of resentment, as the Hindu teaching on forgiveness and atonement, as the Qur'anic teaching on repentance and forgiveness, as the Sikh teaching on confession and forgiveness, as the Confucian teaching on admitting faults and non-retaliation, and as the African understanding that confession brings healing and forgiveness restores harmony.

